mod:redef_reroot_store_prices;
// 2026-11-16 (landing 177d2b9, row 4, the tests row: no source change; it pins rows 1-3, the stack, by verdicts). Row 2 (DEF-685's D5) marks a
// pointer parameter its callee re-points (`pp = p2`; also through its own slot, the call road or a branch) and reads that parameter's chain by
// the marked key. Row 3 (DEF-644 root B, S4) reroots an address taken through another pointer (`r = @(<-q0)` over `q0 = @pp`; `@((<-pp).q)`) to
// that pointer's targets, and `rrti_path`'s and `rrti_chain`'s descents read the rerooted targets' chains by row 2's marked key. So a store
// through such an address in a callee is recorded on what the caller passed only when both rows are in: the stack records what no single row
// records. A fix only adds records beside main's.
// THE PRICES (13), DEF-690 (LOW; introduced by the stack, row 3 on row 2), each a right program running 67 on main (acb78ea) and on every single
// row, refused here, off parity: in a callee, a pointer parameter re-pointed (`pp = p2`), its address taken (`q0 = @pp`) and an address taken
// through that (`r = @(<-q0)`), then a store into the slot or through it (`<-r = p3`, `setp(r, p3)`, `put2pp(r, v)`), is recorded as a write of
// the whole pointee of the parameter's argument, so a caller holding a view into it (`@(m.own[0i64])`) is refused at the call. Remedy: take the
// address by name (`r = @pp`), or store through `q0` directly. Each price's twins run 67 here and on main (redef_reroot_store_ok.npk). A fix must
// tell a store INTO the slot from one THROUGH it and keep every face of redef_reroot_store_faces.npk closed: the first direction named for
// DEF-690 (D5's own-slot cut on row 3's rerooted descent) reopened 24 of the stack-only faces and is withdrawn. The prices: `x_m1a1s1_p2`,
// `x_m1a2s1_p2`, `x_m1a4s1_p2`, `x_m1a1s3_p2`, `x_m1a2s3_p2`, `x_m1a4s3_p2`, `x_m1a1s5_p2`, `x_m1a2s5_p2`, `x_m1a4s5_p2`, `x_m2a1s1_p2`,
// `x_mba1s1_p2`, `sk_s2p_ok`, `sk_p690_br_ok`.
// 2026-11-18 (landing 177d2c, row 2 as F-c: rulings l.17976, l.18021 and l.18074). Row 2 walks a pointer parameter's own slot THROUGH at a call's
// first targets, where main cut it, since the callee may write below it; a store made by name keeps main's cut. Row 2's INTO form, which told a
// store INTO the re-pointed slot from one THROUGH it and ran 10 of the 13 prices above, is withdrawn (l.17940, l.17976): no skip of a walk main
// makes can be shown safe while DEF-685's and DEF-348's lines are open, and the INTO lift is re-planned after they close. The 13 stand as on main,
// 6 of them now at parity: `x_m1a1s3_p2`, `x_m1a2s3_p2`, `x_m1a4s3_p2`, `x_m1a1s5_p2`, `x_m1a2s5_p2` and `x_m1a4s5_p2`, whose direct twins
// `x_m1a0s3_p2` and `x_m1a0s5_p2` are refused at the same site here (this file). Added (6), prices at parity of row 2 (rulings l.16636):
// `x_m1a0s5_p2`, `x_m1a3s5_p2`, `x_m2a0s5_p2`, `x_m2a3s5_p2`, `x_mba0s5_p2`, `x_mba3s5_p2`, each 67 on main and refused here where the plain forms
// of its store are refused on main. Added (8): 7 prices at parity (rulings l.18074), where a callee writing its pointee alone (`setp`'s `<-sp =
// v`), handed the re-pointed slot by name, through an identity call or one hop down, is read as one that may write below it: `x_m1a0s3_p2` (moved
// from redef_reroot_store_ok.npk) and `x_m1a3s3_p2`, `x_m2a0s3_p2`, `x_m2a3s3_p2`, `x_mba0s3_p2`, `x_mba3s3_p2`, `sk_p690_cs_ok`, each 67 on main,
// refused here at one BORROW-015, as main refuses each one's by-name and one-hop twins; and the by-name twin `x_m1a0s3_nm`, refused on main and
// here at the same site, beside its price.
// 2026-11-18 (landing 177d2c, row 3). Added (51): the 47 row-3 faces' own controls (each face less its growth), prices at parity, each 67 on main
// and refused here at one BORROW-009 where its by-name twin is refused on main; `pk2_lc_ok` and `r21_pkt_ok`, moved here from
// addr_via_pointer_store_ok.npk (rulings l.17362), each followed by its direct twin (`pk2_lc_dr_ok`, `r21_pkt_dr_ok`). `c6_mv_rr_sl7_ok` and
// `c6_mv_rr_sl8_ok` are at parity with `c5_mv_bn_sl1_ok`; parity with their own by-name twins waits on DEF-698.
error:E5;
// PRICE OFF PARITY, DEF-690 (LOW; introduced by the stack, row 3 on row 2): a right program, 67 on main (acb78ea), row 1, rows 1-2, S4 (row 3
// alone, on main) and rows 1-3 read by main's key in row 3's descents (O0, O2, roads 0-2, the detector); refused here at one BORROW-015, at `@m`
// in `discard(raw gx(@m0, @m, @m3, hq, n));`. The callee: `pp = p2; HPO->->:q0 = @pp; HPO->->:r = @(<-q0); <-r = p3; pass 7i64;`; the caller's
// view: `e = @(m.own[0i64]);`. Its twin, 67 here and on main: `x_m1a0s1_p2` (`pp = p2; HPO->->:r = @pp; <-r = p3; pass 7i64;`)
// (redef_reroot_store_ok.npk).
